 "poem": "The sky is on her; she glides along,\nShe leads a swan in the water's glow,\nAnd with an air of sweet, old delight,\nA few long-sought outswings go.\nThe moonlight hangs over her,\nAnd her bosom gleams like gold upon,\nAnd a dew falls in golden\nCircles from her body.\nOn her breast and around her body\nThere are blossoms of morning dew,\nYet none flower the flower.\nBut a silver beauty",
